---
import darkSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/words-per-state-dark.svg?raw';
import lightSvg from '../../assets/diagrams/words-per-state-light.svg?raw';
import Diagram from './Diagram.astro';
---

<Diagram
  lightSvg={lightSvg}
  darkSvg={darkSvg}
  maxWidth={680}
  caption="UI words per screen state under the browser benchmark's counting rules (order data, keycaps, and two-word symptom tiles excluded), as locked that Sunday night. Each state's count became its exact CI budget against a 15-word target; the two over it say why in the test file, and the floor fixes later raised several budgets. Training lesson states carry a separate 12-word coaching ceiling."
>
  A broken-axis horizontal bar chart comparing UI word counts across nine screen
  states before redesign or the final trim pass against the CI budgets locked
  that Sunday, with a vertical dashed line at the 15-word target. Tape playing
  dropped from 148 words to 8 (-95 percent), the Fail symptom picker from 34 to
  3, Order ready from 29 to 3, Round 2 ready from 24 to 13, Exception with the
  note open from 21 to 15, Could not inspect with the note open from 20 to 15,
  Inspection result from 18 to 15, Already inspected from 25 to 17, and Round 2 tape from
  25 to 18 (the last two include a 2-to-3-word prior-inspection strip).
</Diagram>
